      "question": "Among the 12 most liquid issuers, which had the strongest and weakest returns over the 20 trading sessions ending August 31, 2026, and how did their daily volatility compare?",
      "submittedAt": "2026-10-01T20:33:02.450410Z",
      "completedAt": "2026-10-01T20:33:35.234750Z",
      "status": "success",
      "report": {
        "markdown": "**Strongest return (top‑ranked)**\n- **Issuer:** **PEAX**\n- **20‑session return:** **+24.74 %**\n- **Daily volatility (σ of daily returns):** **2.91 %**\n\n**Weakest return (bottom‑ranked)**\n- **Issuer:** **VIAS**\n- **20‑session return:** **‑18.78 %**\n- **Daily volatility (σ of daily returns):** **2.60 %**\n\n**Volatility comparison**\n- PEAX’s daily volatility (≈2.9 %) was modestly higher than VIAS’s (≈2.6 %).\n- Both volatilities are low‑single‑digit percentages, indicating relatively calm daily price movements despite the large divergence in cumulative returns.\n\n*All figures are from the market‑scan of the 12 most‑liquid issuers over the 20 trading sessions ending 31 Aug 2026.* [1]\n\n## Sources\n\n- [1] Market analytics result — market scan — evidence `hermes-receipt:d433c7842ab6f45dca12e07eabb9e1c77287b00decc4b3e2ff8060860f5cb5a8`",
